## Why not share-alike

This is a deliberate decision, not an oversight. Requiring share-alike would oblige preservation
architects and engineers to release client deliverables that adapt this material — which would stop
them using the corpus at all, defeating its purpose. Reasoning in full:
[docs/06-trust-anchor-and-licensing.md](docs/06-trust-anchor-and-licensing.md) §3.

**Consequence:** CC BY-SA material (e.g. from Wikimedia Commons or Mapillary) **cannot** be absorbed
into this corpus. Such material must be kept in a separately-licensed, separately-tagged collection.

